RISC3D test kit 38 (19 November 2026): contexts that share objects
=================================================================

For WebKit: its drawing library, Skia, draws in several threads at once,
each with its own context, all sharing one set of textures and buffers.
RISC3D 0.12 does that on RISC OS on Linux: a context can share another's
objects (r3d_create_shared), and each thread has its own current context.

In this kit:
  !RISC3D      0.06-1: RISC3D 0.06 and Linux3D 0.06 (V3DRender 0.16, as
               in 0.05-1)
  riscos-risc3d_0.23-1_arm64.deb   Linux's side: rol-3d 0.20
  Share        sharetest: two threads, two contexts sharing a texture,
               a fence, 200 frames each at once; writes ShareResults
  Test, Info   the usual checks, to see nothing else changed

On RISC OS on Linux (the Pi 4)
------------------------------
 1. Unzip RISC3DTest into HardDisc4, replacing the last kit.
 2. In RiSH's Root shell:
      apt-get install /riscos/HardDisc4/RISC3DTest/riscos-risc3d_0.23-1_arm64.deb
    (it restarts rol-3d).
 3. Copy this kit's !RISC3D over HardDisc4.!Boot.Resources.!RISC3D
    (replace it). PackMan will update it from the RISC3D package later.
 4. Restart.
 5. Double-click Share, then Test and Info.

ShareResults should end "sharetest ok", and *RISC3D should say
"contexts can share objects". Please send ShareResults, Results and
InfoResults, and /riscos/3d/log.txt.

On native RISC OS on the Pi 4 (optional)
----------------------------------------
Copy !RISC3D into !Boot.Resources (V3DRender is the same 0.16), restart,
and type RISC3D at the command line: it should still list V3DRender.
Share will say contexts can't share there: that's expected, as native
programs share through Mesa's own V3D driver (riscos-mesa's 20.3.5-23),
not RISC3D's commands. (Test and Info are for RISC OS on Linux.)
